vock for Debian
===============

Privileges
----------

  * --mode kcov requires root and a kernel built with CONFIG_KCOV. Debian's
    stock kernels do not enable it, so this mode needs a self-built kernel.
  * --mode hw (Intel PT / AMD LBR / CoreSight) needs
    /proc/sys/kernel/perf_event_paranoid set to 1 or less, or root.

The coverage shim
-----------------

vock loads /usr/lib/vock/kcov.so into the traced process with LD_PRELOAD. It
is a private helper, not a public library: it has no SONAME and no stable ABI,
so it is not in the linker search path. Override its location with
VOCK_KCOV_SO if you need to.

selftest
--------

"vock selftest" builds kernels with virtme-ng and shells out to make, so it
expects a source tree and a build toolchain. It is a development aid and is
not expected to work from the installed package.

 -- Yunseong Kim <yunseong.kim@est.tech>
